{"episodes":{"207951":"A prolonged period with significant precipitation occurred on the 13th until the 17th due to a series of systems that brought abundant moisture. Many San Joaquin Valley locations received around 1-3 inches of rain for that period, and the Sierra Nevada foothills, as well as the Sierra Nevada below the snow line, received around 3-6 inches. Snow levels varied from around 8,000 to 9,500 feet from the 13th until the 16th, then lowered to around 5,000 feet by the 17th. The Kern County mountains received a few inches of snow towards Frazier Park on the 17th and 18th, mainly at elevations above 5,000 feet. However, rain fell at the lower elevations, as well as along Tejon Pass towards Lebec. Many Kern County locations received 1 to 2 inches of rain in the San Joaquin Valley and the Kern County desert, while about 2-4 inches of rain fell in the mountain areas.","208052":"Low pressure moving in from the Pacific advected in near-record precipitable water for November, fueling heavy rain and flooding.","208779":"An Atmospheric River in the middle of November brought light mountain snow, widespread rainfall with roadway flooding, gusty winds, and thunderstorms from November 12th through November 14th. Around 1 to 4 inches of rain were observed across interior northern California over this 48 hour period. Gusty southerly winds of 25 to 65 mph were also observed as well. 4 to 12 inches of snow was estimated to have fallen at the highest peaks, generally above 8000 feet in the Sierra Nevada, mainly south of US Highway 50.","208937":"A strong area of low pressure impacts southern California with heavy rain, debris flow, flooding, and gusty winds across the higher terrain.","211615":"A powerful early-season winter storm brought significant rainfall to Southwestern California. Rainfall totals ranged from 2 to 8 inches across coastal and valley areas with 6 to 12 inches across the foothills and mountains. With such rainfall totals, significant reports of flooding were received."},"events":[{"begin":"2025-11-15T02:54Z","county":"Sacramento","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2025-11-15T06:54Z","endLat":38.6223,"endLon":-121.4544,"episode":208779,"id":1300386,"injuries":0,"lat":38.6249,"location":"1.87 NNE Del Paso Hgts","lon":-121.4563,"narrative":"Sacramento Fire Department reported that two people and one dog were stuck on an island at Arcade Creek in Sacramento as waters were rising due to heavy rain. This resulted in a swift water rescue.","source":"Fire Department/Rescue","state":"CA","type":"Flood","wfo":"STO"},{"begin":"2025-11-15T13:38Z","county":"Los Angeles","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2025-11-15T15:00Z","endLat":34.4117,"endLon":-118.5767,"episode":211615,"id":1322186,"injuries":0,"lat":34.41,"location":"1 N Valencia","lon":-118.58,"narrative":"California Highway Patrol reported flash flooding on Interstate 5, just north of the city of Valencia.","source":"Law Enforcement","state":"CA","type":"Flash Flood","wfo":"LOX"},{"begin":"2025-11-15T14:15Z","county":"Los Angeles","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2025-11-15T16:00Z","endLat":34.0374,"endLon":-118.7027,"episode":211615,"id":1322187,"injuries":0,"lat":34.0353,"location":"1 WNW Malibu Beach","lon":-118.7026,"narrative":"California Highway Patrol reported significant flash flooding with all lanes of Malibu Canyon Road flooded.","source":"Law Enforcement","state":"CA","type":"Flash Flood","wfo":"LOX"},{"begin":"2025-11-15T14:37Z","county":"Ventura","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2025-11-15T16:00Z","endLat":34.2737,"endLon":-119.2845,"episode":211615,"id":1322168,"injuries":0,"lat":34.2734,"location":"1 WSW Ventura","lon":-119.2837,"narrative":"Heavy rainfall generated flash flooding on Highway 101. California Highway Patrol reported flash flooding on Highway 101 at the Sanjon Road Offramp. Up to 18 inches of water was reported at t